{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Low-Temperature Network Model.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Low-Temperature Network Model.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"low temperature network model low temperature network model","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Low-Temperature Network Model.md","fileName":"Low-Temperature Network Model.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Low-Temperature Network Model","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-27 18:30\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Local LLM Network Engineering]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Local LLM Network Engineering","Network Modelfile","ainetworkingcookbook.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Low-Temperature Network Model.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Low-Temperature Network Model.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"low temperature network model low temperature network model","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Low-Temperature Network Model.md","fileName":"Low-Temperature Network Model.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Low-Temperature Network Model","heading":"Low-Temperature Network Model","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A low-temperature network model is configured to favor repeatable, high-probability continuations. This is useful when producing Cisco syntax, documentation fields, or automation code where unnecessary variation makes comparison and testing harder.\n\nLow temperature narrows sampling but cannot repair an unsuitable model or incomplete context. A repeatable wrong command is still wrong. The setting belongs in a versioned [[Network Modelfile]] and should be evaluated with known cases so its effect can be distinguished from prompt, model, and dataset changes.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Local LLM Network Engineering","Network Modelfile","ainetworkingcookbook.pdf"],"properties":[